// spec: FUN-013, VAR-007
//
// Two subprograms of one name OVERLOAD when their signatures differ, and are a
// duplicate when they do not.
//
// ⚠️ The parameter types alone decide.  A return type does not distinguish an
// overload: selection happens from the arguments, so two subprograms differing
// only in what they return could never be told apart at a call.
//
// ⚠️ The parameter NAMES do not distinguish them either -- these two claim the
// same signature.

function F (N : Integer); begin Exit 1; end
function F (M : Integer); begin Exit 2; end
